(Phase 1: Planning and Reviewing the Original Brief) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
13 TL
(What we were trying to do: before writing a single line of code, read the original) Tj
T*
(project brief carefully and honestly point out anything missing in the plan itself,) Tj
T*
(rather than assume it was ready to build from.) Tj
T*
T*
(What we actually built: a real 15-day day-by-day plan, a choice of tools \(Python,) Tj
T*
(a face-detection library called MediaPipe, a face-matching library called) Tj
T*
(DeepFace, and a simple local database called SQLite -- all free and able to run) Tj
T*
(on a normal laptop\), and a daily log so every decision was written down at the) Tj
T*
(time, not remembered later from memory.) Tj
T*
T*
(The real problem we found: the brief did not say which sets of face photos,) Tj
T*
(called datasets, should be used to test the system, did not explain how to pick) Tj
T*
(the exact sensitivity numbers \("thresholds"\) the checks should use, and its) Tj
T*
(definition of success was vague -- something like "acceptable performance") Tj
T*
(instead of an actual number to aim for.) Tj
T*
T*
(How we fixed it: rather than guess, we picked specific, named datasets for) Tj
T*
(specific jobs, and committed to measuring real numbers from real test photos to) Tj
T*
(set every threshold, instead of picking numbers that simply felt reasonable.) Tj
T*
T*
(What changed as a result: every number used later in this project -- thresholds,) Tj
T*
(pass rates, error rates -- can be traced back to a real measurement, not a guess.) Tj
ET
endstream
