<< /Length 3000 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
72 740 Td
13 TL
(Separately, in some frames the same face angle produced two different,) Tj
T*
(opposite-looking answers -- for example, reporting a face as turned left when it) Tj
T*
(was actually turned right.) Tj
T*
T*
(How we found it: this was caught by testing against real recorded footage of a) Tj
T*
(person moving their head, not by reasoning about the code -- the mismatch) Tj
T*
(between what the screen showed and what the system reported was immediately) Tj
T*
(obvious once real video was used instead of a handful of still photos.) Tj
T*
T*
(How we fixed it: the root cause was a mismatch in coordinate conventions -- the) Tj
T*
(3D reference points and the coordinate system the underlying math library) Tj
T*
(expected were not lined up the same way, so the numbers coming out were) Tj
T*
(technically correct answers to the wrong question. This was fixed by correcting) Tj
T*
(the coordinate setup itself, not by adding a rule to flip the answer when it) Tj
T*
(looked wrong, since patching the symptom would not have stopped the same bug) Tj
T*
(from causing different, harder-to-spot errors elsewhere.) Tj
T*
T*
(What changed as a result: head-angle detection became accurate and consistent) Tj
T*
(across real test footage, and this fix mattered beyond just this one check -- the) Tj
T*
(same angle numbers are reused for the head-turn liveness challenge in Phase 3.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
