BT
/F1 10 Tf
72 740 Td
13 TL
(Layer 2: an active challenge -- the system asks the user to do something live,) Tj
T*
(such as blink or turn their head, and checks that a real, sustained movement) Tj
T*
(actually happened, using the head-angle math from Phase 2 and a measurement) Tj
T*
(of how open or closed the eyes are, frame by frame.) Tj
T*
T*
(Layer 3: a heartbeat check called rPPG \(remote photoplethysmography -- a) Tj
T*
(method of detecting a heartbeat from video alone, with no sensor touching the) Tj
T*
(skin\). Every heartbeat pushes a tiny, invisible pulse of extra blood through the) Tj
T*
(skin, very slightly changing its color in a rhythm matching the heartbeat. A) Tj
T*
(printed photo or a screen replay has no real blood flow, so this signal simply) Tj
T*
(does not exist in a fake.) Tj
T*
T*
(Why three separate layers instead of one: research in this field shows that) Tj
T*
(systems relying on only one method of checking liveness can be fooled, and we) Tj
T*
(proved this ourselves directly rather than just citing outside research. When) Tj
T*
(Layer 2 \(the blink/head-turn challenge\) was tested on its own against a) Tj
T*
(recording of a real person's real blink, played back as a video, the system) Tj
T*
(accepted it as a live blink, because the challenge only checks whether the) Tj
T*
(correct movement pattern happened on screen, and a recording of the correct) Tj
T*
(movement looks identical to the real thing. This is exactly why the system does) Tj
T*
(not rely on Layer 2 by itself, and combines it with the other two layers instead.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
