(Phase 5: Mentor Feedback That Caused a Real Redesign) Tj
T*
/F1 10 Tf
13 TL
(What we were trying to do: get outside, critical feedback on the design partway) Tj
T*
(through the project, rather than only self-review.) Tj
T*
T*
(The original design: quality checks worked as six separate, rigid pass-or-fail) Tj
T*
(gates -- a photo either passed every single one of six hardcoded cutoffs,) Tj
T*
(scattered across different parts of the code, or it was rejected outright, with) Tj
T*
(no middle ground.) Tj
T*
T*
(What the mentor flagged: this design is hard to explain to a client, since there) Tj
T*
(is no single number to point to, and impossible for a client to adjust) Tj
T*
(themselves. Not every user has a good camera or good lighting -- a rigid) Tj
T*
(all-or-nothing gate that works fine in a bright test might reject many real users) Tj
T*
(on an ordinary webcam in a dim room. Figure 4, next page, shows the redesign.) Tj
ET
endstream
